cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  rare-target-prioritization: a reproducible pipeline for therapeutic target
  prioritisation in rare monogenic disease, demonstrated on CIPA
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it as below, and cite the underlying
  public resources listed in DATA_SOURCES.md.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Simone Edoardo
    family-names: Candelo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5741-574X"
    affiliation: University of Pisa
abstract: >-
  A pipeline that proposes and ranks candidate therapeutic targets for a rare
  monogenic disease from public resources only, keeping human curation as a
  declared downstream step and reporting what it cannot know. Demonstrated on
  congenital insensitivity to pain with anhidrosis (CIPA, NTRK1). No
  experimental validation.
keywords:
  - target discovery
  - rare disease
  - CIPA
  - NTRK1
  - Open Targets
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-13"
